Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 09:34:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?robo(downloads):=20Reference=20Sheet=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=E2=80=94=20a=20design's=20latest=20run,=20summarised?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adds a separate "Reference Sheet" section to the Downloads page: one Design
Name field that finds the design's LATEST production run and downloads a
one-page Excel summary — the reference to check before running that design
again. Existing Complete Production / Delay List downloads are untouched.

Design matching is by name only, thickness ignored: "Costa 2 cm" and
"Costa 3 cm" are one design (Costa), while "Bellagio Green" and "Bellagio
Grey" stay distinct (designMatchKey strips only a trailing thickness token).
No production for the design → "No previous production record found".

The sheet is a summary, one item per row: Production Date (first slab),
Batch Number, Design Name, Thickness, Total Slabs, Total Production Time,
Total Delays, Avg Slabs/hour, Robo Program Names (only Robos actually set up
for the run) and Robot Delays (the G-category delays that occurred, blank if
none). Total Slabs / Total Production Time / Total Delays reuse the exact
Reports helpers (count, productionSpanMinutes, summed durationMinutes) over
the run's slabs, so they equal what Reports shows for that run.

Avg Slabs/hour uses the approved Reference-Sheet formula with delays
SUBTRACTED: Total Slabs ÷ (batch duration − actual delay time), where the
actual delay time is the UNION of the delay intervals (mergedDelayMinutes)
so overlapping downtime is not removed twice. This is the one figure that
intentionally differs from the Reports KPI, which leaves delays in.

Pure, tested helpers (referenceSheet.ts: designMatchKey, mergedDelayMinutes,
avgSlabsPerHourNet — 16 node --test cases); the DB half (referenceData.ts)
is shared by the preview API and the Excel export so screen and file can
never diverge. stampMinutes is exported from productionSpan.ts for the delay
interval anchoring. No schema or DB change.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
